# Cloudflare Pages response headers (ignored as a plain file everywhere else).
#
# COOP/COEP make the site cross-origin isolated, which enables
# SharedArrayBuffer — required by the pthreads-built vampire.wasm. These are
# the same two headers serve.sh sends locally; GitHub Pages cannot send them,
# which is why the Vampire backend only works on the Cloudflare deployment.
# Cache-Control: no-cache means "store, but REVALIDATE with the server before
# every use" — after a deploy, the next load gets the new files immediately
# (unchanged ones come back as cheap 304s). Without it browsers heuristically
# cache the un-hashed app.js/wasm and users see stale builds until a forced
# refresh. If assets ever get content-hashed filenames, those can switch to
# long-lived immutable caching instead.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Cache-Control: no-cache
